  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="35">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIIAtr">VIII Atr</ref> 35</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="35" corresp="#wit-d">Cristenum mannan gebirað swiðe rihte þæt he Godes abilgðe wrece swiðe georne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">It is the duty most incumbent upon a Christian man that he should avenge offences against God with the utmost diligence.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Christlichem Menschen [König Cnut] geziemt sehr mit Recht, dass er Beleidigung gegen Gott sehr ernstlich bestrafe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">It very rightly befits a Christian man [king, Cnut] to avenge offences against God very zealously.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">‘mannum’ is wrong according to what follows; II Cn 40.2 has ‘cyninge’ (Liebermann). Liebermann compares VIII Atr 2.1.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
